     1	//! `Intl.DurationFormat`-compatible formatting (P7-01d).
     2	//!
     3	//! Patterns and separators come from the frozen generated table (`duration_data.rs`,
     4	//! Node 24 / ICU); locale resolution mirrors `crate::locale`, plural categories —
     5	//! `crate::plural`, digit grouping — `crate::format`. Contract:
     6	//! `waves/RW-30/TZ-W30a.md`.
     7	//!
     8	//! Semantics: units are emitted in the fixed order years → months → weeks → days →
     9	//! hours → minutes → seconds → milliseconds, zero units are skipped, an all-zero
    10	//! duration yields `""`. Each unit is rendered as its CLDR template for the cardinal
    11	//! plural category of the exact integer magnitude (no `f64` round-trip, so values
    12	//! above 2^53 keep every digit and their category). Separators are frozen per
    13	//! locale/style: `join2` for exactly two units, otherwise `join_middle` between the
    14	//! leading units and `join_last` before the final one.
    15	//!
    16	//! Fallback chain: requested (canonical + enabled) → `en-US` row → `"{n} {unit}"`.
    17	//! NNBSP/NBSP are normalized to a plain space in the output (as in `render_pattern`).
    18	//! The function never panics, including on `u64::MAX`; there is no `unsafe`.
